---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";

/*
 * ariada.org/patents — patent-pending statement.
 *
 * SPDX-License-Identifier: EUPL-1.2
 *
 * Public-facing transparency page stating filed-IP positions and
 * the EUPL-1.2 Article 2 patent-peace grant for downstream OSS users.
 * Per-application specifics (application numbers, filing dates, claim
 * counts) are intentionally omitted from this surface; they are
 * available on request to EU/EEA residents via legal@ariada.org and
 * authoritatively at the USPTO Open Data Portal.
 *
 * patent-audit-skip: this page was deliberately collapsed to a plain
 * patent-pending statement. It carries no application numbers and no
 * portfolio codenames, so there is nothing to geo-fence — the disclosure
 * wrapper is intentionally absent.
 */
---

<Base
  title="Patent status — ariada.org"
  description="Agonist Development AB holds filed, patent-pending IP positions covering accessibility-compliance algorithms. Downstream OSS users receive patent peace under the EUPL-1.2 Article 2 grant."
>
  <section aria-labelledby="patent-status-heading">
    <h1 id="patent-status-heading">Patent status</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Agonist Development AB holds filed, <strong>patent-pending</strong>
      intellectual-property positions in the United States covering
      accessibility-compliance algorithms.
    </p>
    <p>
      Downstream open-source users receive <strong>patent peace</strong>
      for the published OSS surface under the
      <abbr title="European Union Public Licence">EUPL</abbr>-1.2
      Article&nbsp;2 grant. The licence grants each user a royalty-free,
      non-exclusive right to any patents held by the licensor to the
      extent necessary to exercise the rights granted on the Work.
    </p>
    <p>
      Per-application details (application numbers, filing dates, claim
      counts) are available on request to
      <abbr title="European Economic Area">EU</abbr>/<abbr title="European Economic Area">EEA</abbr>
      residents via
      <a href="mailto:legal@ariada.org">legal@ariada.org</a>.
      Authoritative records live at the
      <a href="https://data.uspto.gov/apis" rel="external">USPTO (United States Patent and Trademark Office) Open Data Portal</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="patent-peace-heading">
    <h2 id="patent-peace-heading">What patent peace means for you</h2>
    <p>
      If you use, fork, or redistribute the EUPL-1.2-licensed packages
      published under <code>@ariada-org/</code>, you receive an
      irrevocable, royalty-free patent licence covering the maintainer's
      filed positions <em>to the extent necessary</em> to exercise your
      EUPL-1.2 rights on the released Work. You are not at risk of
      patent-infringement claims from Agonist Development AB for that use.
    </p>
    <p>
      The &ldquo;to the extent necessary&rdquo; language is deliberately
      narrower than the Apache-2.0 or
      <abbr title="Mozilla Public Licence">MPL</abbr>-2.0 patent grants.
      It covers OSS use of the published code; it does not extend to
      commercial rebuilds or derivative services that step outside the
      licensed Work.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="links-heading">
    <h2 id="links-heading">Related pages</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><a href="/architecture">System architecture</a> &mdash; the OSS component map</li>
      <li><a href="/licenses">Licence matrix</a> &mdash; per-package SPDX identifiers and rationale</li>
      <li><a href="/legal/patent-peace">Patent non-assertion pledge</a> &mdash; the canonical, binding pledge for OSS users</li>
      <li><a href="/about">About</a> &mdash; maintainer and stewardship statement</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="muted">
      Maintained by Alexander Brichkin (Agonist Development AB,
      Sweden, org.nr 559452-5726).
    </p>
  </section>
</Base>
